#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166718 :question/id #uuid "03bebdcd-5908-5c60-b35a-1c8f59593afd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9577" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f4f0de23892a6f76642f8c7e5d3a6112a8ffa2d9f50000cd974f293a7d8b3b6.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-1)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^2 + (y - (-1))^2 = 2^2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx^2 + (y+1)^2 = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166719 :question/id #uuid "04c9673b-e4e5-508d-acc7-ea0888f2cf87" :question/math-academy-id "e-9578" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3895bafe045f7e460887aee41bf390fdda753fed87eaab14f4a29ddb792267c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{2^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{4^2} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \\dfrac{x^2}{4} + \\dfrac{y^2}{16} = 1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166720 :question/id #uuid "58850b39-db80-532d-9f60-808a215da76c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9579" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a92eae1ab0af29ea895b570c95199ece1e292c09953ebb2dabbb7c6e2d422d6c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,-2).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny^2 = 4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x = 3$ and $y = -2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\ny^2 = \\dfrac{4}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d76abaf-d6f3-5b89-8bc8-773822409c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x^{2}}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163625} {:answer/id #uuid "af7463aa-12d7-57ad-803b-3c850c3fe265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163626} {:answer/id #uuid "ca72da31-eeea-56d4-973b-8125561d7056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163627} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2d3c03-496e-55bf-a039-5ecbd04ee38f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163628} {:answer/id #uuid "06dcb89b-43af-580e-a84a-316afd26beda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yx^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163629}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fff66644-0b05-5c26-a65d-0ffc27452391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163624}] :question/id #uuid "3d859e7f-f28f-5c06-af6e-a805a7402be0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127359" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efaa81ed608cd130b1f9a6000dd50c27f8d81ed7cbd6c10570c04df1281c149d.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the circle shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdffde0b-6618-51d6-bc49-a22477f723f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y - 1}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163631} {:answer/id #uuid "d1dfdf67-527b-511d-abee-249d1eb9a880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x + 1}{y - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163632} {:answer/id #uuid "27c4a1e8-5acb-5b6f-8de6-b2f50aeb90c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y - 1}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163633} {:answer/id #uuid "38683bd4-b061-5d5a-a1c0-60944a2fa2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x - 1}{y + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163634} {:answer/id #uuid "38ae922f-61ca-5b33-bdae-7d7e14ba332a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x + 1}{y + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163635}] :answer-field/id #uuid "02b4c5ff-6289-5b8b-bb00-03fbd4292b64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163630}] :question/id #uuid "ef223789-79d4-59f3-b94f-8f0a66169b59" :question/math-academy-id "q-127360" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a09aa5c81ec7775f390901569afb0468204c49752eb401845e6836317616f25d.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the circle shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3ad7cd7-53ee-50c6-991d-7d73a0f6743a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163637} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3df2cb-6a20-5d32-8269-e7e4d022249d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163638} {:answer/id #uuid "0813c0d3-82a8-5058-a03d-c618284e99e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163639} {:answer/id #uuid "46c3927c-367a-5b92-ab69-0a1993e45431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163640} {:answer/id #uuid "7ebe77cd-3662-58ce-b781-4d6dd8b29dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163641}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd20f05-fcd1-55c1-8286-a5e170cba952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163636}] :question/id #uuid "feee00f3-146d-53ba-a889-b1572bbf7d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127362" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f74e1bfe8c53edb73d22633aa3bbf59f5046ebf793541dac8cbcf35127b72601.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the ellipse shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8de18c-3f57-5375-af7f-efa2e0197549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(y+1)}{4(x-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507652} {:answer/id #uuid "a673094f-6307-5b33-92bf-06c740822bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507832} {:answer/id #uuid "db7d24c3-d19d-5779-b9b1-949d29cf47df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9(y+1)}{16(x-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507894} {:answer/id #uuid "f0580d29-12ed-56aa-ba70-461fe3aa6008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507923} {:answer/id #uuid "f95d1962-8d93-5d37-a3ac-481ea9ea1974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-2)}{3(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a673094f-6307-5b33-92bf-06c740822bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507832} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae32260f-36b3-5a38-a8ce-a21db00f57c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "321fa992-8b54-51c4-9c6a-89b1f36a3444" :question/math-academy-id "q-127364" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b56ff4cb47d9b529762c6364eac2eed4b666c7ca9eab6f6ba7d3bc161387433e.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(2,-1)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-2)}{9}+\\frac{2(y+1)}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y+1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-2)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0573536-31f0-563b-9d07-911863e634bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163649} {:answer/id #uuid "d09192f8-b86c-51d6-a122-7afcd699607f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163650} {:answer/id #uuid "d9efdc1d-d656-5d1e-83d6-ccd7d0ea85d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163651} {:answer/id #uuid "f4600882-36d2-52ce-8da2-b54d8b2af6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163652} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3b5a55-f245-5539-8b5a-59cf6f8686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163653}] :answer-field/id #uuid "41202eeb-84d9-576f-9f59-f15c773b23c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163648}] :question/id #uuid "0981d1d8-5908-5954-92c8-10f4e8de0d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127372" :question/problem "![](images/00/0030e466a772b1ccd61140453c5e0e50ff365a0bf42034422bce9e1691983c43.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b50d0c40-6788-57f6-abfc-e79bf313d479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163655} {:answer/id #uuid "0872fa03-25f1-5ab1-8e8a-b7add5e28113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163656} {:answer/id #uuid "40308631-4569-53b4-a049-a0c1e9473978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163657} {:answer/id #uuid "515e1940-de9b-5005-bcc4-522fce4979f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163658} {:answer/id #uuid "77251aea-0d1b-53cd-8e9c-1840b159150c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40308631-4569-53b4-a049-a0c1e9473978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163657} :answer-field/id #uuid "106254b3-fb7a-53e5-9145-bedbc3b56b87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2b2fc0d7-ecff-5b63-8ad8-a6faaff8e7b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127374" :question/problem "![](images/88/88bec66b7ece961f2f0fc4083ce317f2bdc414e0a219d61bbf9bf73ae667ca0f.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-2,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2675139a-3fa5-5b56-94e2-c392744f2058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260211} {:answer/id #uuid "53dc176a-f425-5b28-938a-cb3b8dfbea9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260581} {:answer/id #uuid "705192e6-bac2-5c6b-acc2-b4a6d7c27a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260862} {:answer/id #uuid "e9942a87-c77c-5a9d-a10f-bfd1dc59e1f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261919} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2aee2c-79cc-5487-8a09-2deff11502b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9942a87-c77c-5a9d-a10f-bfd1dc59e1f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261919} :answer-field/id #uuid "486a8e80-f3f5-5ea0-86c4-8514e424260b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fdc8e2a5-3885-5dd5-9725-cf793a052578" :question/math-academy-id "q-127493" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f24d078ca0dc57ebd12778b7862683b0289e9c0d4c664639bd210dcc1f7c6d1b.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={4}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(16) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1baa187c-702f-5d74-9e49-a1dc869d9fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260112} {:answer/id #uuid "5a6d8273-ae12-56d9-9e8e-fcc50fc83290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260645} {:answer/id #uuid "74a22088-ee78-5010-84ba-740de0945199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260896} {:answer/id #uuid "ae28886d-9cbf-5b7c-9d76-cf9e7ca1aa9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(x+1)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261410} {:answer/id #uuid "e6444082-8e18-513f-a526-e008b7c933af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a22088-ee78-5010-84ba-740de0945199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260896} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d6fbea-23c2-5931-a1d8-e65fc956b604" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262313}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "270ef110-70fe-5fce-83a6-6d6bf6a5f7cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-127497" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a3ca092dc7c0668ac465d4832b91a2b831af057ff22e357b4e7105bfb454ea18.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(1,0)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2}={2}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086f2ce1-1368-53f8-ba86-97532f17e2be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x+1)(y+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259953} {:answer/id #uuid "15624327-92e2-5e45-93c8-9e8b0f12c8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-x}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260061} {:answer/id #uuid "1b0ad15c-3fd9-513f-9213-0034cf18a310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{1-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260109} {:answer/id #uuid "262a7584-90ba-501c-94ba-193aab3a5f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x+1)}{y-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260210} {:answer/id #uuid "56f957aa-f127-5fa0-8b32-8a16dec1aaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)(1-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b0ad15c-3fd9-513f-9213-0034cf18a310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{1-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260109} :answer-field/id #uuid "d01c7489-9aff-5d6d-85e8-5b918e133134" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262489}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d49ad33a-9c4d-534a-b2d2-deca2d37a9d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-127499" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f08e0a0d1fd855f2d179ac65dbdf5d022f3488b85c78b5cbb507f12bd69487e.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(-1,1)$ and has a radius of $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={1}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)+2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{y-1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+1}{1-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cbff705-86d7-5620-9b91-f217fc3dd62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259995} {:answer/id #uuid "1404812d-8afd-556d-a934-1872662ba5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260050} {:answer/id #uuid "2cae2188-2835-52aa-8873-60409aaec2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x-3)}{y-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260276} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7c9e2c-eda0-5eef-8879-0d607c2ec01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260952} {:answer/id #uuid "86c7e6c8-e96b-5be4-8744-21b6d321d35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(y+2)}{x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1404812d-8afd-556d-a934-1872662ba5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260050} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ab4b98-7df7-574e-9078-9c3fc81e2000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8fba4c03-ae99-5394-bb2d-645b07038e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-127500" :question/problem "![](images/78/78ad1a6835bb71441f77a3ca2bbdc93a42635e0386cda35fbe5fc9b0c9f48677.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(-3,-2)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2}={2}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+2)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+3)+2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12fcdc1d-9e23-5008-bf5d-34dc22fc186c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260042} {:answer/id #uuid "22b7ceba-bd0d-5cf4-99c5-b69358079cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y+2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260179} {:answer/id #uuid "41bc10c8-5d61-5860-b083-a238754518aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+2}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260450} {:answer/id #uuid "79ec63bb-645a-50e8-b0a6-bd5548a8649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260940} {:answer/id #uuid "97f828a2-e540-5264-bff8-1e86698e24a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ec63bb-645a-50e8-b0a6-bd5548a8649a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260940} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9b4da9-c684-5fbe-a09a-8174d70bd535" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49f66e90-d770-50de-8b81-b5c4a9d9e022" :question/math-academy-id "q-127502" :question/problem "![](images/81/812f88e913650b7924fc13acc7adde999819d0011fa547a7e0ad73cb37e3939f.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-2)$ and has a radius of $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2}={3}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+2)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "219845eb-d05c-53b6-8c35-514bf8a6a3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260163} {:answer/id #uuid "2cbaa061-8eee-52ef-b708-518d83dacbe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260277} {:answer/id #uuid "6a53e920-1f56-54ef-9a0d-a07c822f8f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260807} {:answer/id #uuid "6f270028-5c9b-5ad1-bf83-211b5d81af31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260852} {:answer/id #uuid "d675cc22-4e88-5836-a463-6a2f29d37cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cbaa061-8eee-52ef-b708-518d83dacbe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260277} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac39f57-fa34-5bb6-bec8-a47660173164" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d5970e3a-67be-579a-8f6a-680fce2bb7ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-127510" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e0d18f7db92cfbe372f998e69d2395f2d586eb36cd25773588149c4ccf678eba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,6).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(3,6)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=12x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{6}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193eadf3-4d9d-5560-876d-95d6202e9c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260095} {:answer/id #uuid "35d44e75-ae76-5b88-839e-6d033a89f631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260357} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1dc785-7cef-5337-90f3-1ba825d33fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260694} {:answer/id #uuid "76364d2a-ee13-58e3-90a7-aedf8b7a207f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260907} {:answer/id #uuid "85fa198d-352f-536a-a28b-55a7d967de78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f1dc785-7cef-5337-90f3-1ba825d33fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260694} :answer-field/id #uuid "f89dbf13-8c69-578f-a637-7a5acc775b45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "adf3739c-b726-56b2-925a-36974745f33e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127511" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c0295c7cdc1abc16273efda842a0aa7a892ece2f5dda5e29f7baab25320b23ec.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\right) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1140d60d-8a60-5b24-9707-fdbbe10ee174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{25x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260030} {:answer/id #uuid "4928b8e7-3c13-5270-9da7-dbed823cec42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5y}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260508} {:answer/id #uuid "898d463a-7dfd-5838-ad1a-295cc8ef06dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261076} {:answer/id #uuid "cd48c351-7d51-5019-b57c-50ccdbfa2e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{25y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261684} {:answer/id #uuid "e37eac43-a53e-522f-a6fb-5b0bac1c7603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{5y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd48c351-7d51-5019-b57c-50ccdbfa2e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{25y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261684} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c0aa41-e415-529b-aa04-ad06f0391b13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4ab32aff-f9ee-5a7b-b7ab-1cf6d27aabda" :question/math-academy-id "q-127512" :question/problem "![](images/43/43e8ed1ee117ccd10f0e3aa03fc8db8ec1db6c076689e9072e1e22e048dfc279.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $5$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{25}+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{25y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183fee6d-7bac-5669-b5aa-f2ca1c2bd40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260087} {:answer/id #uuid "2282148e-42ae-5ff6-bce6-30eb16686d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260177} {:answer/id #uuid "916a9d4b-7d6d-5152-a204-c68e617838a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5y}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261138} {:answer/id #uuid "9bcc7b58-ed39-578e-82a9-0c547be35fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261225} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c686f5-6e36-5c65-8a51-b8412271e0e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183fee6d-7bac-5669-b5aa-f2ca1c2bd40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260087} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a57a652-58c5-59d0-92fb-d161ba76dd70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fb8ad6d7-f6da-5fbc-be48-a49f26e33603" :question/math-academy-id "q-127513" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f8effaf21270245ed6f8df63d2e430483756f47537b1c7325e88acc5286544db.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $5,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{25x}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1c1e34-b587-5bca-a469-20c953d57e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260270} {:answer/id #uuid "693786d3-819f-5b02-b1be-af3f39567b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260794} {:answer/id #uuid "9090e1a2-9626-5a06-becc-3f269eff1a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261133} {:answer/id #uuid "a67e3b39-983b-5712-8fb5-9b1da10418c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261326} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ba3065-ceff-5d5a-b70f-f705a5bbfc51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "693786d3-819f-5b02-b1be-af3f39567b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260794} :answer-field/id #uuid "86e3dd0a-3fde-5ff0-95a9-90f1ef3e0463" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9b971938-bd81-5d73-bed8-1323d79a80ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-127514" :question/problem "![](images/54/547b79b566d2914db4a63997cd5fc9f02dd1517b8dcd5e53cde8c07ac5ca05a2.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $3$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{9}+2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53b126be-2e72-5683-87f0-2bce708ce0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260580} {:answer/id #uuid "ac29313d-f700-5356-b3ea-db25827d7000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261378} {:answer/id #uuid "af2deb81-9196-5179-b2ff-4e88fe6ffef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261420} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ee63f7-23d8-539c-8477-779c46a531e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261595} {:answer/id #uuid "d1164fca-4cb8-5220-a316-6ca8fe78ed20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b126be-2e72-5683-87f0-2bce708ce0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260580} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c21556d-ce63-50ba-aa4c-f313d47a9e13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b2ff195e-41e9-5105-9c9e-ed134d28a53d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127515" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5eedb15e515993bdc8a2ee37ab4c7c0e0225b9d2118d5d60e8593de5ea56f199.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05cc5c38-3fac-504b-a52a-dbbcc512e957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259926} {:answer/id #uuid "46b94c76-6f4b-5df7-afa2-245210c1a600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260489} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac2c1f5-97e4-55ee-8c09-94a6ec7fc43d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260651} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc8ab5c-9f98-553d-8e5c-4e7a8e4f49d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260970} {:answer/id #uuid "aa32c440-9d05-5e9e-95fc-705f2a3492a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46b94c76-6f4b-5df7-afa2-245210c1a600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260489} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb45d64f-7844-5746-b5c9-fba237c20fd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "72fb768f-c740-5cf4-b10e-4551f1d715de" :question/math-academy-id "q-127520" :question/problem "![](images/60/60987d053d138d4a26cbc05adccb0da23810f97243f9399d3fe401a0202394b0.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-8,4).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-8$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4851ac26-61ba-5347-9f08-d47ae995e612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260501} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4961c6-6f8c-5abb-ae07-f2b8f05a2801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y-1}{4(x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260551} {:answer/id #uuid "73d79fd3-f240-55a0-b25f-2433c34e6adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y+1)}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260888} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dc3e16-f6aa-54b9-855f-a4bf2e902cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{4(y-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261353} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd86f62-82c8-517d-b725-1ed0ece0565b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x+1)}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4851ac26-61ba-5347-9f08-d47ae995e612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260501} :answer-field/id #uuid "e478fe35-cddc-5025-b3b3-364a777b1da3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8af60131-dadd-5b8a-b5a0-d50b94e5f35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127523" :question/problem "![](images/eb/ebef81911a434828ab94e643007d06b677538cdf0995198c7a065e35a8f81996.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,-1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{4}+2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e42ef4c-5447-5bff-960b-4b0d7b21d724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y-1)}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260539} {:answer/id #uuid "5c45f41e-d062-5f9f-b16d-79174ef52362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(y-1)}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260662} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec4a30f-fd49-5493-92c9-d0c013da0e11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{2(y-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261252} {:answer/id #uuid "c5590232-b5fa-5ba7-9564-1bf4158a2bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261617} {:answer/id #uuid "d902d09a-c34e-56e1-b99d-14fc0f75c8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{9(y-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5590232-b5fa-5ba7-9564-1bf4158a2bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261617} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa189a6-0586-58c4-bdad-b279c7fe8ea4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3bb11842-6e3d-5501-86bf-db20e32986e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127525" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb0fbc8f57621946a5ec5168e8c607d230269e0c6a64b4c86c835c110f0f6288.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(0,1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2(y-1)}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(y-1)}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2265eb9b-3ab7-561c-9e8b-bbb0f82b1df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3y}{2(x-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260173} {:answer/id #uuid "357f7559-50b2-593c-8d89-5de3d3f5f3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x-3)}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260353} {:answer/id #uuid "398e1764-a4b7-5a3c-928e-904cdefd12f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y-3)}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260391} {:answer/id #uuid "7f214ada-9d01-5ad3-b18e-86c992bd8801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{4(y-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260979} {:answer/id #uuid "d3513ebf-6544-564b-be5d-1eb3dcfba194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3513ebf-6544-564b-be5d-1eb3dcfba194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261734} :answer-field/id #uuid "b98f98c2-9a67-5e94-9d12-ac8be15735e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "32df6ca6-168d-529a-bf6d-352a5419e7a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-127526" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4c39b409f6049a4fdead506c329d232820876c37ede9540adfeade2d7c1b9dc.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(3,0)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-3)}{9}+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-3)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f6ba14-67bb-52a5-83f3-90748a808eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18f6ba14-67bb-52a5-83f3-90748a808eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295413} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea47b69-ba23-5df0-89cb-9a0a8a5b3195" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2b5b23fa-be02-551f-968d-c9191c07be80" :question/math-academy-id "q-312780" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b269001ff5a3a1a1d86125157ee2f5b77d89ebcf0041f8d403dbc931b796c5e8.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(5,7).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ and $y=7$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 49 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{49}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{5}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{49}{5}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{10y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ce1afa-8b88-5a8a-8cdc-4e464a1bb102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315162} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ad31bfe-fcf5-5162-a8e6-4281f1f124b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "28f921c8-6fd7-5d79-b2ff-0d1df567197f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342215" :question/problem "![](images/c4/c403f11093b76facafbecb72bcc413640ac67fe6ed73d6b64374230f39e29aba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-1).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-1$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\ 1 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad5bf0a8-9d5e-50fe-96f9-d4d663d3f517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5bf0a8-9d5e-50fe-96f9-d4d663d3f517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316094} :answer-field/id #uuid "12408f4c-1370-5d9b-b3b2-f660b8736202" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a43aa514-b6a3-516e-bf25-cd1e713491f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-342218" :question/problem "![](images/73/7367cb4ae1feb4e18b98b712687ceb4a1db67f8c9e4965af3ffd1253a827f346.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-6x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-6x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4203b15d-0bea-5e2b-934d-26d20084a739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4203b15d-0bea-5e2b-934d-26d20084a739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315503} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd3bd66b-afeb-5b87-8ae5-7c88b3e0adad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3b67c83b-c5b3-5c60-b778-f810479299ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-342354" :question/problem "![](images/85/85d75e0f3a9f2a30282d1f1754b0c46da49e8f73ff2a858c856ba5492eb21cca.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(8,-8).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=8$ and $y=-8$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b26c1af7-9a5b-5d43-b1b5-dc74de3adf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b26c1af7-9a5b-5d43-b1b5-dc74de3adf12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316127} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a041cb-28c3-51b4-b579-c9bbf60ee415" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c82bb467-368a-5a4c-94f6-b887899fd25e" :question/math-academy-id "q-342355" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1aab10c5376ca6ae6c43829bc6f7617fb236b24c883d8ad61c47b83b75511d5a.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(6,-2).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=6$ and $y=-2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 4 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4825a0cb-b3fb-5323-8a58-511f26bf6c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(y-2)}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503116} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6a63f8-ed2d-5275-9398-6d460d70e710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x+1)}{y-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503196} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfcca81-3430-5271-8cd0-80e5d2035124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{4(x+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503241} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c781b7-f9f3-553f-b0be-cf3d3b1d44f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503376} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b72652-cf0b-559e-99bc-226911189b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{2(y-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5c781b7-f9f3-553f-b0be-cf3d3b1d44f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503376} :answer-field/id #uuid "88db5750-a4d8-5c4f-b26f-ef8a62130a02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1e5b95a8-8914-5efe-a3ab-4b5dce1c8cbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-127521" :question/problem "![](images/e7/e74f96531b57a877b043ac4302adae6beef90dc24d64efc8e1a24b563e4738b7.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,2)$ and has semiaxes $4$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{16}+\\frac{2(y-2)}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y-2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{4(y-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5efdb2c0-9881-5a00-b565-3f359e70c7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507737} {:answer/id #uuid "93f161f4-832c-5426-af71-c7778005d5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507807} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a24980-5105-538e-8c74-64c4ebc803d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3y}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507904} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c9d2d6-91af-5536-9214-6c10a18ce267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507909} {:answer/id #uuid "ef20abea-8c5e-5aa2-aa09-5d4772fb2a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef20abea-8c5e-5aa2-aa09-5d4772fb2a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507922} :answer-field/id #uuid "293366ad-ad39-5d08-a9c8-a7c1154b5526" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3f2a3f8a-3c25-5094-b1ff-9932bec29ec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-127503" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c6a99f62a77f7fc16dbb95e8a8d03c42b266fffee10ed3739ab13820729be44.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(2,-3).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 9 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{9}{2}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{9}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518103 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7532c1eb-1150-5b3d-abb1-342bec35e705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7532c1eb-1150-5b3d-abb1-342bec35e705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517710} :answer-field/id #uuid "87ca15d6-48a6-50a1-9d31-763d81685807" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0343bcd3-e974-592d-9f5b-2241e197ca26" :question/math-academy-id "q-131253" :question/problem "Given that the point $(2,\\sqrt{5})$ lies on the graph of $y={f}^{′}(x),$ find ${f}^{″}(2).$\n\n${f}^{″}(2)\\,=\\,$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({f}^{′}(x))\n$$\n\nis the slope of the tangent line to the graph of $y={f}^{′}(x).$ \n\nNotice that the graph of $y={f}^{′}(x)$ on $x\\in [-3,3]$ is a semicircle of a radius $3$ centered at $(0,0).$ Its equation (for $y>0$) is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2}={3}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(2,\\,\\sqrt{5})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "055f7f68-8860-5fcd-ba89-65573245d570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536053} {:answer/id #uuid "2a5b1be4-7c6e-5722-a2f4-2aa1b2aae130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536054} {:answer/id #uuid "6675c608-2d79-51da-8ce1-3d915d6d59c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536055} {:answer/id #uuid "6e160412-70c4-5898-9627-1e775d2346d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536056} {:answer/id #uuid "8c584b97-62a0-5d84-bf7d-5b2abde11f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c584b97-62a0-5d84-bf7d-5b2abde11f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536057} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc377f79-c91d-5163-84d3-cf26a1ed63ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d7a2ead7-a103-561d-ae19-16273e0e5510" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4efe76bd06d22c5735b427c150f5a09b7288f8281b90921aeb11902c864176e5.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\right) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101bc44b-ae63-5792-a272-b928410c2e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545116} {:answer/id #uuid "46ee26ff-f58f-5032-b7db-ac117f845487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545130} {:answer/id #uuid "5dffa1dd-a4d5-5af7-920b-9642c3173a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545138} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4529a6-2047-5774-a2c8-a00d35e21602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545158} {:answer/id #uuid "dba2bb78-136a-54a8-971a-c8bf7500191a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab4529a6-2047-5774-a2c8-a00d35e21602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545158} :answer-field/id #uuid "b87ecf42-e1b6-5f2d-940c-a6c537ae74ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0075b464-322a-5f3d-9f7e-e9a5a8363cca" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3da6e664f55c8abb41ff05e3f7e7108ab1f7c648e887402885347eccd42ed46.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={3}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a3fc09a-efc9-5c4c-ac65-bd75198800e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545131} {:answer/id #uuid "7db5b616-54c4-5818-91bd-8636dfe89f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(x+\\frac{7}{2})}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545143} {:answer/id #uuid "8677d2a0-5832-5a14-aa54-22f821cce209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545148} {:answer/id #uuid "a92aeace-c06b-57c2-b93a-99dd15e0cb20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{2(y+\\frac{1}{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545156} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb38e3c-a97d-5d21-b693-c4de60dd22b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y+\\frac{1}{2}}{x+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8677d2a0-5832-5a14-aa54-22f821cce209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545148} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3406e35-cfa3-57be-b127-de08e9b94e52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4baaba62-d9ac-5b3e-89d5-fbd516aa665c" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4ca74438b4c5e5eeae2ce46d7a86964d74adfb1e12df6029a41a04c0dea7e93.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(- \\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{1}{2})$ and has a radius of $\\frac{3}{2},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right))^{2}+(y-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right))^{2}={\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+\\frac{7}{2})+2(y+\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cc9736-1ad6-592a-aebb-e6c16d0d50e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545113} {:answer/id #uuid "1c75beaa-b238-5161-9628-8a764302e2cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545117} {:answer/id #uuid "236ef634-16e5-560d-8f85-33280287b1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(x+\\frac{7}{2})}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545120} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3d80d9-4059-5ed3-acb0-dc16dbea0388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y-\\frac{1}{2}}{x+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545140} {:answer/id #uuid "b6245221-7e9b-5bd2-b04e-69243f16c537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{2(y-\\frac{1}{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03cc9736-1ad6-592a-aebb-e6c16d0d50e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545113} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ed4e09-8541-5487-a559-d5ce5f6c3312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "81a754d2-b653-5f5c-a94e-7ee027cc6ddf" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3ea6262a334d81630f0d8c1b35654c7d3c74745a344587be73b1852015ed3f47.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle